  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \r\rDesign and Access Statement\r25/486/01\r25/486/02\rHeritage Impact Statement\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The extended nursery hereby approved shall be occupied by no more than 36 children at any one time.\r\rReason: To prevent harmful intensification of the site and to ensure the proposed use does not prejudice the enjoyment of neighbouring occupiers of their properties.\r",
    "The additional rooms hereby permitted for the nursery use shall not be occupied until details of 4 long-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\rThese details should demonstrate:\r\ro In an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m.\ro Design: accessible to all and meet recommended space requirements,\ro Secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob.\ro Fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r\r",
    "The outdoor play space as shown on the approved 'Location Plan' shall only be used for children's play by no more than 9 children at any one time and in accordance with the schedule attached between the hours of 10:00 to 11:30 and 14:30 to 16:00, Mondays to Fridays only, excluding Bank Holidays.  \r\rAGE\t          MAXIMUM NUMBERS\t\tTIMES\r0 - 2 years\tNo more than 9\t          10:00 - 10:30\r2 - 3 years\tNo more than 8\t          10:30 - 11:00\r3 - 4 years\tNo more than 7\t          11:00 - 11:30\r\t\t\r0 - 2 years\tNo more than 9\t          14:30 - 15:00\r2 - 3 years\tNo more than 8\t          15:00 - 15:30\r3 - 4 years\tNo more than 7\t          15:30 - 16:00\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining properties.\r",
    "The additional rooms hereby permitted for the nursery use shall not be occupied until a Travel Plan for the development has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rThe travel plan should demonstrate:\ro Trip generation to and from the development.\ro How the development will cope with increased trips.\r\rOnce approved, the development shall operate in accordance with the Travel Plan for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure that the development complies with Enfield DMD Policy 48.\r",
    "The additional rooms hereby permitted for the nursery use shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the increased occupation of the development have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities are to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r"
  ],
